>Carter</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Killick-Kendrick</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><source>Rodent malaria</source><year>1978</year><publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>245</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>A.S</given-names></name><name><surname>de Roode</surname><given-names>J.C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sim</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>A.F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Within-host competition in genetically diverse malaria infections: parasite virulence and competitive success</article-title><source>Evolution</source><volume>60</volume><year>2006</year><fpage>1358</fpage><lpage>1371</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16929653</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bremermann</surname><given-names>H.J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pickering</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A game-theoretical model of parasite virulence</article-title><source>J. Theor. Biol</source><volume>100</volume><year>1983</year><fpage>411</fpage><lpage>426</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/0022-5193(83)90438-1">doi:10.1016/0022-5193(83)90438-1</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6834864</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>M.C</given-names></name><name><surname>Donnelly</surname><given-names>C.A</given-names></name><name><surname>Alpers</surna